      "math_academy_id": "q-355385",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Let $S=\\{-3,-1,2,4\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(-3)=5,\\,f(-1)=1,\\,f(2)=1,\\,f(4)=8.\n$$\n\nCompute ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x).$\n\n$\\,$\n${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$ {{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $5,$ $1,$ $1,$ and $8,$ so the minimum output value is $1.$ This minimum occurs at both $x=-1$ and $x=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)=1\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)=\\{-1,2\\}.\n$$",
